<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seychelles</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Seychelles is an archipelago in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>, which was a British colony from the early nineteenth century. The British used it as a place of exile for deposed rulers. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a> note that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asantehene">Asantehene</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prempeh-i">Prempeh I</a> was exiled to the Seychelles after the British occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumasi">Kumasi</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seychelles.jpg" alt="Seychelles" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Vxb83 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Seychelles.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
